  "question": {
    "text": "The light of two different frequencies whose photons have energies <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>eV</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>eV</mi></math> respectively, illuminate a metallic surface whose work function is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>eV</mi></math> successively. The ratio of maximum speeds of emitted electrons for the two frequencies respectively will be :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
